Object.assign(dict.en,{
 guide1Title:'Prepare the measurement',guide1Text:'Use the same detector and consistent container, fill height and counting geometry for samples and the efficiency standard. Record the net sample mass accurately. Ra/Th rely on daughter lines, so sealing and equilibrium time must follow the laboratory method.',
 guide2Title:'Select the efficiency standard',guide2Text:'Use the built-in standard for the supplied project samples only when their measurement geometry matches. For other data, upload a traceable standard measured with the same detector and geometry as the samples. Verify the source certificate before changing mass, activity or reference date.',
 guide3Title:'Import sample spectra',guide3Text:'Files may be .xls, .xlsx or .txt, and multiple samples can be selected together. The spectrum must contain recognizable channel-count data. TLIVE, live-time fields or derivable timing metadata are read automatically; enter live time manually when none is detected.',
 guide4Title:'Enter analysis settings',guide4Text:'Enter each net sample mass in grams and review the reference date, ROI half-width, background gap and window width. Enter a manual slope and intercept only when reliable calibration coefficients are known; otherwise leave them blank for per-spectrum auto-calibration.',
 guide5Title:'Run quantitative analysis',guide5Text:'Select “Run quantitative analysis”. The system parses spectra, fits E = a × CH + b, locates Ra/Th/K lines, estimates local linear background, calculates net count rates, and derives specific activity and content by matched-geometry comparison.',
 guide6Title:'Read the results',guide6Text:'Summary shows ppm, potassium percentage, Bq·kg⁻¹ and multi-sample comparison. Process Detail retains peak position, gross, background and net counts. Sample Spectra & Fits shows raw spectra, matched calibration points and fitted lines.',
 guide7Title:'Complete quality review',guide7Text:'Review correlation R, deviation, RMS, usable line count and all warnings. R close to 1 indicates linear association only; it does not by itself prove correct peak assignment or quantification. Investigate calibration residual, equilibrium, dead-time or peak-count warnings against source data and lab records.',
 guide8Title:'Choose language and export',guide8Text:'Choose Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, English, or French, then export PNG, PDF or Excel. PNG/PDF include result tables, activity comparison, per-sample calibration-fit curves and peak analysis. Excel also contains editable fit charts, process data, line references and method/QC records.',
 guideTroubleTitle:'Troubleshooting',guideTroubleText:'If analysis fails, check that the file structure and columns are recognizable, live time and mass are positive, standard and samples use matched geometry, and enough clear calibration peaks are present. Re-run analysis and export after corrections.',
 guideContactTitle:'Author contact (feedback and suggestions)',guideContactText:'twinkle-air  Email: twinkleair369@gmail.com  or twinkle-air@qq.com',
 guideNote:'Important: this tool supports calculation and review; it does not replace sample preparation, sealed equilibrium, source traceability, instrument QA or laboratory approval.'
});
